-- title:
--   Weil reciprocity for f against a function from the base field
-- statement:
--   Let $K \subseteq F \subseteq F'$ be a tower of fields ($F'$ an $F$-algebra, $F$ a $K$-algebra, scalars compatible) with $F'/F$ finite and separable and $F$ of characteristic zero, and suppose that both $F/K$ and $F'/K$ have principal divisors: every nonzero element has a finitely supported integer-valued divisor on the set of places (valuation subrings containing $K$, proper, with principal ideals) whose value at each place $v$ is $v.\mathrm{ord}$ of the element, and which has degree zero. Assume `WeilReciprocity K F`, i.e. for all nonzero $f_0,g_0 \in F$ with divisors $D_{f_0},D_{g_0}$ given placewise by the orders, with $\mathrm{ord}_v f_0 = 0$ or $\mathrm{ord}_v g_0 = 0$ at every place $v$ and with both supports consisting of rational places (places whose residue field is generated by the image of $K$), one has $D_{g_0}$-evaluation of $f_0$ equal to $D_{f_0}$-evaluation of $g_0$, where evaluation of $h$ at $D$ means $\prod_v (\text{residue of } h \text{ at } v)^{D(v)}$, the residue being taken in $K$ and set to $0$ when $h$ lies outside the valuation subring. Let $f \in F'$ and $g \in F$ be nonzero, and let $D_f, D_g$ be divisors of $F'/K$ with $D_f(w) = \mathrm{ord}_w f$ and $D_g(w) = \mathrm{ord}_w(\mathrm{algebraMap}\,g)$ for every place $w$ of $F'/K$. Assume that at each such $w$ either $\mathrm{ord}_w f = 0$ or $\mathrm{ord}_w(\mathrm{algebraMap}\,g) = 0$; that every place in the support of $D_f$ is rational; that every place of $F/K$ is rational; and that for every place $v$ of $F/K$ with $\mathrm{ord}_v g \neq 0$, all places in the fibre of $v$ in $F'$ are rational. Then the $D_g$-evaluation of $f$ equals the $D_f$-evaluation of $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,g$.
--
--   This is Weil reciprocity on $F'/K$ in the special case where the second function comes from the base field $F$, obtained by reduction along the finite separable extension $F'/F$; the rationality hypothesis on all places of $F/K$ is stronger than rationality on the support of $D_g$ alone. It feeds the general Weil reciprocity statement [`AlgebraicCurve.weilReciprocity`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.weilReciprocity).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_weilReciprocity_algebraMap.lean

